{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-02-Feb-2026-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 23, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The mode of the observations 22, 21, 22, 20, 33, 34, 22, 29, 29, 31, 23, 23, 28, 32, 22, 26 and 27 is:", "options": [{"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "22"}, {"n": 2, "text": "A computer printed 1,76,400 lines in a given day. If the printer was in operation for 6 hours during the day, how many lines did it print per minute?", "options": [{"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "490", "added": false}, {"text": "420", "added": false}, {"text": "460", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "490"}, {"n": 3, "text": "In △ ABC, BD ⟂ AC at D and ∠ DBC = 66°. E is a point on BC such that ∠ CAE = 35°. What is the measure of ∠ AEB?", "options": [{"text": "65°", "added": false}, {"text": "59°", "added": false}, {"text": "47°", "added": false}, {"text": "66°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": "59°"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The difference between the present ages of two sisters is 3 years. After 2 years, the elder sister will be twice as old as the younger sister was 2 years ago. Find the sum of their ages after 8 years from now.", "options": [{"text": "33 years", "added": false}, {"text": "39 years", "added": false}, {"text": "31 years", "added": false}, {"text": "37 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "37 years"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The ratio of three numbers is 12 : 21 : 5. If 50 percent of the first number is 78, then what would be 50 percent of the absolute difference of third and second number? 5000", "options": [{"text": "105", "added": false}, {"text": "103", "added": false}, {"text": "102", "added": false}, {"text": "104", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "104"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A, B and C can do a piece of work in 3, 9 and 18 days, respectively. How long (in days) will they take to do twice the same work, working together?", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": "12 m/s"}, {"n": 7, "text": "If 4 lines of a print, in a column of a book, contain 36 words, how many words will a column of 50 lines contain?", "options": [{"text": "454", "added": false}, {"text": "446", "added": false}, {"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "460", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "A"}, {"n": 8, "text": "X, Y and Z together can complete a piece of work in 8 days, while X alone can complete it in 24 days and Y alone can complete it in 36 days. Find in how many days Z alone can complete the work?", "options": [{"text": "48 days", "added": false}, {"text": "12 days", "added": false}, {"text": "18 days", "added": false}, {"text": "28 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "18 days"}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "6"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹4,000 at 6% per annum rate of interest for the period from 22 February 2024 to 23 April 2024.16", "options": [{"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 11, "text": "In a town with 75,000 voters, 95% cast their votes, all of which were valid. There were three candidates: A, B, and C. Candidate A received 40% of the valid votes, while candidate B received 12% fewer votes than A. What percentage of the valid votes did candidate C receive?", "options": [{"text": "52%", "added": false}, {"text": "48%", "added": false}, {"text": "15.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "24.8%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "24.8%"}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "18.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "16.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "15.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "14.67%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "16.67%"}, {"n": 13, "text": "The volume of a sphere is numerically equal to its surface area. Find its radius (in units).", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 14, "text": "A computer printed 1,76,400 lines in a given day. If the printer was in operation for 6 hours during the day, how many lines did it print per minute?", "options": [{"text": "450", "added": false}, {"text": "490", "added": false}, {"text": "420", "added": false}, {"text": "460", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "direct-inverse-variation", "key_answer": "450"}, {"n": 15, "text": "If P : 17 :: 42 : 6, then find the value of P. 4875", "options": [{"text": "116", "added": false}, {"text": "119", "added": false}, {"text": "122", "added": false}, {"text": "118", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "119"}, {"n": 16, "text": "The value of the expression is _____.", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "0.1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "10% loss"}, {"n": 17, "text": "A vertical stick 15 m long casts a shadow 5 m long on the ground. At the same time, a tower casts a shadow of 46.5 m long on the ground. The height of the tower is:", "options": [{"text": "137.5 m", "added": false}, {"text": "141.5 m", "added": false}, {"text": "139.5 m", "added": false}, {"text": "135.5 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "heights-and-distances", "key_answer": "139.5 m"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Find the effective price percentage of the marked price after three consecutive discounts of 11%, 18% and 20% (rounded off to two decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "58.88%", "added": false}, {"text": "62.14%", "added": false}, {"text": "61.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "58.38%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": "58.38%"}, {"n": 19, "text": "During the festive season, one large laddoo having radius 32 cm is made as prashad. After pooja, it is decided to make small laddoos from one large laddoo so as to distribute to the devotees. How many laddoos of radius 2 cm can be made?", "options": [{"text": "4132", "added": false}, {"text": "4096", "added": false}, {"text": "3896", "added": false}, {"text": "3964", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": "4096"}, {"n": 20, "text": "The value of the expression is _____.", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "0.1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "100"}, {"n": 21, "text": "A person saves 10% of his income. If his expenditure is ₹360, then his income (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "400", "added": false}, {"text": "440", "added": false}, {"text": "324", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "400"}, {"n": 22, "text": "A, B and C can do a piece of work in 3, 9 and 18 days, respectively. How long (in days) will they take to do twice the same work, working together?", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "4"}, {"n": 23, "text": "Rahul covers a distance of 225 km in 15 hours. How many hours will he take to cover 40% less distance if he drives 20% faster than his original speed?3164", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5", "added": false}, {"text": "8.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": "7.5"}]}